    "title": "Rep. Shontel Brown criticizes Trump pardons in series of tweets",
    "text": "Congresswoman Shontel M. Brown | Shontel M. Brown Official Website\nCongresswoman Shontel M. Brown | Shontel M. Brown Official Website\nRep. Shontel Brown, a U.S. Congresswoman representing Ohio’s 11th district, posted a series of tweets on January 7, 2026, alleging that former President Donald Trump pardoned multiple individuals she described as fraudsters and scam artists.\nIn her first tweet at 18:11 UTC, Brown stated: \"This one’s a fraudster: https://t.co/p0cW4qzAF8\".\nA minute later, she continued with another post: \"Here’s another scam artist he pardoned: https://t.co/via6P1i3Nc\".\nIn a third tweet at 18:11:17 UTC, Brown added: \"And another one… Trump has pardoned too many fraudsters to count: https://t.co/mUtNmhTAuD\".\nShontel Brown has represented Ohio's 11th District in the U.S. Congress since 2021 after succeeding Marcia Fudge. Before joining Congress, she served on the Cuyahoga County Council from 2015 to 2021 and was born in Cleveland in 1975. She currently resides in Warrensville Heights and holds a Bachelor of Science degree from Wilberforce University.",
